{
  "id": "walls___no__of_studs",
  "title": "Walls - No. of Studs",
  "description": "Calculate required number of studs in a wall based on wall length and center distance between studs.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Calculate the number of studs required in a wall using the formula: n = L / l + 1, where n is the number of studs, L is the length of wall, and l is the center distance between studs.",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "wall_length",
          "label": "Wall Length (ft)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 16,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "stud_spacing",
          "label": "Center Distance Between Studs (ft)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1.33,
          "unit": "ft"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "num_studs",
          "label": "Number of Studs",
          "formula": "inputs.wall_length / inputs.stud_spacing + 1",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Formula\n\n**n = L / l + 1**\n\nWhere:\n- **n** = number of studs\n- **L** = length of wall (ft, m)\n- **l** = center distance between the studs (ft, m)\n\n## Note\n\nAdditional studs are required in corners and around doors and windows. This calculation provides the base number of studs for the wall run."
    },
    {
